  "headline": "Indonesian Police Link Former Chief to Illegal Surveillance Case",
  "seoTitle": "Police Link Former Chief to Illegal Surveillance",
  "metaDescription": "Indonesian police officials have linked former police chief Listyo Sigit Prabowo to an illegal surveillance operation targeting President Prabowo Subianto.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Police Chief Suyudi Ario Seto accused former chief Listyo Sigit Prabowo of ordering illegal surveillance against the president.",
    "Bareskrim investigators have conducted a search at the residence of the former police chief regarding the ongoing investigation.",
    "Eight witnesses involved in the case have requested official protection from the Witness and Victim Protection Agency (LPSK)."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "During a parliamentary working session, National Police Chief General Suyudi Ario Seto detailed findings regarding an unauthorized surveillance operation targeting President Prabowo Subianto and other national figures. Allegations suggest that former Police Chief Listyo Sigit Prabowo acted as the primary end user for the operation, purportedly receiving daily intelligence reports from Irjen Slamet Uliandi. The investigation into the incident has led to the detention of multiple suspects, including home confinement for one individual. Furthermore, investigators from Bareskrim Polri have executed a search warrant at the former police chief's residence to secure evidence. Amid the ongoing probe, the Witness and Victim Protection Agency (LPSK) confirmed it has received applications for protection from eight witnesses connected to the case. Authorities have outlined five distinct stages of the illegal surveillance operation as the legislative and judicial inquiry continues.",
